hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8205","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Yunus Al-Dhabi told us, Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdad told us, Sufyan, and Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Ahmad bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He said: “Indeed, God Almighty has not sent down a disease without sending down a cure for it. He taught it to those who knew it, and ignorant of it to those who were ignorant of it.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it, and the origin in this matter is the hadith of Usama bin Sharik, which the two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, attributed to the fact that they did not “They find a narrator for it on the authority of Usama bin Sharik other than Ziyad bin Ulaqah.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8205 - True"
"8206","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Tanafisi told us, Mas’ar told us, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i, and Abdullah bin Muhammad told us. Al-Saidalani, they said: Muhammad bin Sulaiman bin Al-Harith told us, Khallad bin Yahya told us, Mas’ar told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Amr told me Al-Bazzar in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Musa al-Qurashi told us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, Mas’ar bin Kadam told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Osama bin Sharik, may God be pleased with him, said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Bedouins asking him. They said: O Messenger of God, we are upon us. Are we embarrassed by such-and-such? Are we embarrassed by such-and-such things? For things in which there is no harm. Then he said: “Servants of God, God has placed the burden on us, except for those who commit an act of honour. A Muslim man unjustly, that is the one who was embarrassed and perished.” They said: Shall we seek medical treatment, O Messenger of God? He said: “Yes, seek treatment, servants of God, for God Almighty has not created a disease without creating a cure for it, not just one disease.” They said: O Messenger of God, and what Him? He said: “The old age.” They said: O Messenger of God, what is the best thing that has been given to man? He said: “Good character.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. It was narrated by ten trustworthy Muslim imams, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah. Among them was Mas’ar bin Kadam, as I mentioned earlier about him, and among them was Malik bin Mughal Al-Bajli” [p. 442]:\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8206 - True"
"8207","Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to me, Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa’id narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sa’id narrated to us. Muhammad bin Abi Al-Khanajer, in Tripoli, and he was trustworthy and trustworthy. Muhammad bin Mus’ab Al-Qurqa’i told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Ziyad bin A relationship, and among them is Amr bin Qais Al-Malai:"
"8208","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Abu Bakr, and Uthman, Ibn Abi Shaybah told us, they said: We told him: Jarir, on the authority of Al-A’mash, and among them was Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj"
"8209","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq Al-Basri told us, in Egypt, Saeed bin Amir told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Maslamah bin Ibrahim told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ali Al-Muaddeeb, Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, and Abu Amr Muhammad told me Bin Ja`far al-Zahid al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Muhammad al-Bakhtari told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muadh al-Anbari told us, Ubai told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ziyad Ibn Alaqah, and among them is Muhammad Ibn Juhadah Al-Iyadi [p. 443]:"
"8210","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Sahl bin Ahmad Al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abdul-Quddus bin Muhammad bin Abdul-Kabir narrated to us. Bin Shuaib bin Al-Hijab, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Imran Al-Qattan told us, Muhammad bin Juhadah told us, and among them was Abu Hamza Muhammad bin Diabetic auspicious:"
"8211","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sunni reported on the authority of Marw, Abu Al-Mawjih told us, Abdan informed, Abu Hamza reported on the authority of Ziyad Ibn Ulaqah, and among them is Abu Awanah al-Waddah:"
"8212","Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Harbi told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, and among them was Sufyan bin Uyaynah Al-Hilali:"
"8213","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, Ali bin Hamshadh, and Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, they said: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, and among them was Othman bin Hakim Al-Awdi:"
"8214","Abu Ja`far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Sa`id ibn al-Muddhikir narrated to us, Abu Zur’ah al-Imam narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ulaqah narrated to us, Usama bin Sharik narrated to us, saying: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as if there were birds above our heads. Not one of us spoke when people came to him. Of the Bedouins, and they said: O Messenger of God, give us a fatwa about such-and-such, give us a fatwa about such-and-such, and he said: “O people of the Bedouins, God has made it difficult except for those who He borrowed something from his brother, who was in distress and perished. They said: Shall we seek medical treatment, O Messenger of God? He said: “Yes, God Almighty has not sent down a disease without sending down a cure for it, other than one disease.” They said: What is it, O Messenger of God? He said: “The pyramid.” They said: Who is the most beloved of God’s servants to God? He said: “The best of them in character,” and among them is Shayban bin Abdul Rahman on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, and among them is Zuhair bin Muawiyah Al-Ja’fi:"
"8215","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Khaythamah told Zuhayr. Bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Usama bin Sharik, and among them is Amr bin Abi Qais Al-Razi [p. 444]:"
"8216","Abd al-Samad bin Ali bin Mukarram al-Bazzar told us about him, in Baghdad. Ya’qub bin Yusuf al-Qazwini told us, Muhammad bin Sa’id bin Sa’id told me. Previously, Amr bin Abi Qais narrated to us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, and among them was Muhammad bin Bishr bin Bashir Al-Aslami, who is one of the most trustworthy: Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Nasrabadi told us, Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Duri told us, Abu Ya’la Al-Basri told us, Abu Ya’la Al-Basri told us. Abu Asim,"
"8217","Al-Hakim, may God Almighty have mercy on him, said: I was informed on the authority of Suleiman bin Saif Al-Harrani, on the authority of Abu Asim, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Bashir told us. Al-Islami, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, and among them is Israel bin Yunus Al-Subaie:"
"8218","Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i told us, Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi told me, Abdullah ibn Raja told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, Then he mentioned the hadith. Al-Hakim, may God be pleased with him, said: “I have mentioned less than half of the isnaads of this hadith, for I have traced those who the two sheikhs agreed upon.” May God be pleased with them both for the evidence used in the two Sahih books, and more than half remains in my book for the seeker of this knowledge to contemplate and leave a proverb This hadith, in spite of its attestation and many narrations, indicates that there is no narration of it on the authority of the Companion except one reliable follower who is accepted.” Abu told me Al-Hasan Ali bin Omar Al-Hafiz, may God have mercy on him: Why did they omit the hadith of Usama bin Sharik from the two books? I said: Because they did not find a narrator for Usama bin Sharik other than Ziyad bin Ulaqah. “So Abu Al-Hasan, may God be pleased with him, told me, and he wrote it for me.” In his own handwriting, he said: Al-Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, narrated on the authority of Yahya bin Hammad, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Bayan bin Bishr, on the authority of Qays bin Abu Hazim, on the authority of Mirdas Al-Aslami, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “The righteous will go as ancestors.” The hadith and not Mirdas has a narrator other than Qais, “Al-Bukhari narrated two hadiths on the authority of Zahra bin Ma’abad, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Hisham bin Zahra, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Abdullah has no narrator other than Zuhra,” and they all agreed to narrate the hadith of Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Adi bin Umairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Whoever We appoint to do a job,” and Adi bin Umairah has no narrator other than Qais, “and they all agreed on Hadith of Majza bin Zahir Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prohibiting the meat of domestic donkeys, not by Zahir An undivided narrator,” “Al-Bukhari narrated the hadith of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Amr bin Taghlib, and Amr had no narrator other than Al-Hasan,” “And he also narrated The hadith of Al-Zuhri, “and they all reported the hadith of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Amr bin Taghlib, and he has no narrator other than Al-Hasan,” and the hadith of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, on the authority of Usama bin Sharik is the most correct, the most famous and the most narrated of these hadiths. “Abu Al-Hassan said: Amr bin Al-Arqam narrated, And Mujahid, on the authority of Usama bin Sharik, and this hadith was narrated, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah and Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with them, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “As for the hadith of Jabir [p. 445]:"
"8219","So Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ahmad bin Issa told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He acknowledged that he said: “For every disease there is a cure, so if the cure for the disease is applied, he will be cured, God Almighty willing.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim. And they did not take it out.” As for the hadith of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri:"
"8220","So Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Shabib bin Shaybah told us, Ata’ bin Abi Rabah told us, Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, told us that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God did not send down a disease - “Have He not created a disease - unless He sent down - or created - a cure for it, which He taught it to those who knew it, and who knew it to be ignorant of it, except for the poisonous.” They said: O Messenger of God, and what Toxic? He said: “Death.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8220 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8221","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that a man came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and said: O Messenger of God, my brother complains about his stomach, so he said: “Give him honey to drink.” He said: I gave him a drink, but it only increased his diarrhea, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him, said on the third or fourth: “God has told the truth, and your brother’s stomach has lied.” So he went and gave him a drink and he was healed. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim. And they did not take it out.”\n["
"8222","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa bin Masoud told us, Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “It was When Solomon, the Prophet of God, peace be upon him, stood in his place of prayer, he saw a tree growing in front of him, and he said: What is your name? So you say: Such and such, and he says: What are you for? So you say: For such-and-such, and if it is for a medicine, it is recorded, and if it is for a plant, it is planted. While he was praying one day, he saw a sprouting tree. In his hands, he said to her: What is your name? She said: Carob. He said: What are you for? She said: Because of the destruction of this house. Solomon, peace be upon him, said: Oh God, grant my death to the jinn so that mankind may know that the jinn do not know the unseen. He said: So he carved it out as a stick, and he leaned on it. He said: Then the earth ate it up, and it fell and fell down, and they found him dead, a year old, so the humans realized that the jinn If they had known the unseen, they would not have remained for a year in humiliating torment.” And Ibn Abbas used to recite it like this, and the jinn thanked the earth. “So she used to bring her water wherever she was.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not take it out.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8222 - True"
"8223","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Ibrahim bin Humaid al-Tawil told us, Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar told us, about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam, may God be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of God, incantations we used to seek protection and medicines we used We seek treatment with it. Will it come back from God’s decree? He said: “It is God’s decree.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8223 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8224","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Israel informed us about the pillars Bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Qais Bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Bin Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “You should abstain from cow’s milk, for it sprouts from every tree, and it is a cure for every disease.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8224 - True"
"8225","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The two cures you have to do are honey and the Qur’an.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8225 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8226","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb told us, and Al-Hussein bin Yasar Al-Khayyat told us, they said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aisha, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you has a fever, let him pour cold water over him for three nights as a pre-emptive measure.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8226 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8227","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz did not tell us, Hamid bin Abi Hamid Al-Muqri told us, Ishaq bin Suleiman Al-Razi told us, Al-Jarrah bin Al-Dahhak Al-Kindi, on the authority of Kurayb bin Sulaym, on the authority of his mother, the wife of Al-Zubayr, who said: “When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a fever, He orders us to cool the water, then pour it on him.”"
"8228","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told me, Affan told us, Hammam told us, Abu Hamza told us, he said: I was I push the crowds away from Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both. He said: So I withheld from him for days, and he said: What kept you? I said: Fever, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fever is from the breath of Hell, so cool it with water.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs, and they did not take it out with this increase.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8228 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8229","Abu Abdul Rahman bin Al-Wazir told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Fever is a piece of fire. So cool it off from you with water.”\nHe said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a fever, he would call for a skin of water, empty it over his horn, and take a bath.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not include it with this addition.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8229 - True"
"8230","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Salamah al-Razi told us, Saif bin Muhammad ibn The sister of Sufyan Al-Thawri, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “You should drink the black halij, for it is a tree from the trees of Paradise. Its taste is bitter and it is a cure for every disease.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8230 - Ahmad and others said: The sword of a liar"
"8231","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Husayn, he said: I heard Abu Ubaidah bin Hudhayfah narrates, on the authority of his aunt Fatima, who said: I visited the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with some women, and behold, a waterskin hanging down, And water dripped on him because of the intense heat of his fever, so I said: O Messenger of God, if you pray to God to take him away from you, he said: “Indeed, it is more severe.” “The test of people is the prophets, then those who follow them.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8231 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8232","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Ahmed bin Balawayh told me, Muadh bin Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Saif bin Miskin told us, Abdul Rahman told us Ibn Abdullah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Hasan Ibn Saad, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman Ibn Abdullah Ibn Masoud, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “You should abstain from the milk of cows and their fats, and beware of their meat, for their milk and their fats are a medicine and a cure, and their meat “Disease.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8232 - Saif Wahah Ibn Hibban"
"8233","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist in Baghdad, told us, Yahya bin Hafs bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Bakr bin Ubaid Allah told us. Ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Utba bin Abdullah al-Taymi, on the authority of Asma bint Umays, may God be pleased with On her authority, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked me: “What do you shower with?” I said: With the sunburm. He said: “Hot, hot.” She said: Then I walked in the sunnah. He said: “If there was anything to cure death, it would be in the sunnah.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8233 - True"
"8234","Abd al-Rahman bin al-Hasan al-Qadi told me, Ibrahim bin al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Khaled al-Hudha’, On the authority of Maymun Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take treatment for pleurisy. “With marine costus and oil.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8234 - True"
"8235","Muhammad bin Al-Mu’mil bin Al-Hasan told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Sha’arani told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Nufaili told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ja’far bin Al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that she told him that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when they said: We feared that the one with the Messenger of God had a junub said: “It is from Satan, and it is not God.” So that he may give him authority over me.” This hadith is based on the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. It was narrated on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, contrary to this narration. With a weak chain of transmission.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8235 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8236","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi told us, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Ishaq told us, Ibn Ishaq told us Lahi’ah, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died of a The side\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8236 - It is not valid"
"8237","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Muslim bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Madini, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The The loin is the vein of the kidney. If it moves, it harms its owner, treat it with burning water and honey. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. \"He takes him out\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8237 - True"
"8238","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Hani Al-Adl told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Affan bin Muslim told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped and gave the cuppers “He rewarded him and begged.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not mention it with this addition.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8238 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8239","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told me, Hammad bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, my son This is the excuse. He said: “Do not burn the throats of your children.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8239 - Hammad and Yahya are weak"
"8240","Abu Amr Othman bin Abdullah bin Al-Sammak told us in Baghdad, Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Harithi told us, Muadh told us Ibn Hisham, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Bahrani, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, may God be pleased with him, he said: “I heard the Prophet God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, characterizes oil and warts due to pleurisy.” Qatada said: “He gives birth from his side which ails him.” This is a high hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8240 - True"
"8241","Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad told us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Nadr al-Hurashi told us, Yahya ibn Yahya told us, Issa informed us Ibn Yunus, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon Aisha, and then she A woman was with her boy, who was gushing blood from his nostrils. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is the matter with this?” They said: By him the virginity. He said: “Woe to you, do not kill your children. Any woman whose child is born virginity, let her take an Indian share.” So let her rub it with water and then smear it on him.” Then he ordered Aisha to do the same to the boy and he was healed. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8241 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8242","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuhli told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed, Al-Mish’al told us, Amr bin Muslim Al-Muzani told me, he said: I heard Rafi’ bin Amr Al-Muzani, may God be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The tree and the sticky tree are from Paradise.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not He takes it out.”"
"8243","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hussein bin Muhammad bin Ziyad told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Ju’fi told us, Qais bin Hafs al-Darimi, Talib bin Hujayr told us, Hud bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of his grandfather Mazydah, he said: When we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, They brought out to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one of their dates, and they started eating them. He called those dates by their names, and they said: What are we? O Messenger of God, I know more about its names than you. Then he said to a man: Give us food from the rest of those close to you. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This Al-Barani is the best of your dates, and it is a cure for no disease.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8243 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8244","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub and Ali bin Abdullah Al-Attar told us in Baghdad, saying: Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeeb, Fulayh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Sa’sa’a, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abi Yaqoub, On the authority of Umm al-Mundhir al-Adawiya, may God be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me, and with him was Ali, who was a camel. She said: And we have pending vases. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up and ate, and Ali got up and ate, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Wait, O.” Ali, you are a camel.” So Ali sat down, then I made them chard and barley, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Pour some of this now, O Ali.” A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8244 - True"
"8245","Ahmad ibn Ya’qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf ibn Ya’qub al-Qadi told us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami told us, Mu’tamir ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Umm Kulthum, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “ You should do what is beneficial and obnoxious: the talbinah. By the One in whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, it washes the belly of one of you just as he washes dirt from his face. With water. She said: And when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained, the twine would not remain on the fire until it came to one end of it. Either death or life. “This is a hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8245 - According to Al-Bukhari’s condition"
"8246","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ghassan bin Malik told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Mawwal told us, Ayoub bin Al-Hassan bin Ali bin Abi Rafi’ told me on the authority of his grandmother, Salma, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: He was not a man. He complained to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, of pain in his head except that he said: “Have cupping,” and of pain in his legs except that he said: “puff them.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8247","Ahmad bin Yaqoub Al-Thaqafi told me, Yusuf bin Yaqoub Al-Qadi told us, Abu Al-Rabi’ Al-Zahrani told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, described to them regarding the race of women that They take the calf of a ram, neither large nor small, and it is beaten, then it is divided into three parts, and he drinks a portion every day.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8247 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8248","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym and Ibn Kathir told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of your “Ithimud, for it sharpens the sight and makes the hair grow.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8248 - True"
"8249","Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahan the butcher in Mecca informed me that God Almighty protected it in purity. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz told us. Ahmad bin Yunus, Israel told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He should apply kohl with itthimond three times before he sleeps every night. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it. And servants, no proof was spoken about it.”"
"8250","Abu Nasr Ahmad bin Sahl al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Saleh bin Muhammad al-Hafiz told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Amr told us, Amr told us Bin Al-Numan, Mansour bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Hajabi told us, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with them, she said: An abscess came out on my neck. This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Open it and do not let it eat meat and suck blood.” This is an authentic hadith. chain of transmission, and they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8250 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary\n On the authority of Qatada bin Al-Numan, with a chain of transmission traceable to the Prophet: “If God loves a servant, he protects him in this world just as one of you protects a bottle of water,” according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8250 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8251","Abdullah bin Ja`far al-Farisi told us, Ya`qub bin Sufyan told us, Ishaq bin Muhammad al-Farwi told us, Ismail bin Ja`far told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “I fell ill and my family protected me with everything, even water, so I was thirsty one night and nothing Someone was with me, so I approached a hanging waterskin and drank a drink from it, and I got up while I was healthy, and I became aware of the health of that drink in my body.” He said: Aisha, may God be pleased with her, used to say: “Do not protect the sick person at all.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8251 - True"
"8252","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ahmad bin Issa told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Bukayr narrated to him, that Asim bin Omar bin Qatada narrated to him, that Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with him The masked man returned to them, then said: I will not leave until he is cupped, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is a cure in this.” An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8252 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8253","Bakr ibn Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, in Marw, and Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Qantari told us in Baghdad, saying: Abu Qalaba Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqqashi, and Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Faqih and Ismail ibn Najid al-Sulami narrated to us, saying: Abu Muslim narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, narrated to us Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I have never passed by a crowd of “The angels only ordered me to do cupping.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8253 - Incorrect"
"8254","Ahmad bin Ya’qub al-Thaqafi told us, Yusuf bin Ya’qub told us, Muhammad bin Abi Bakr told us, Sulaiman bin Daoud told us, Abbad bin Mansour told us, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to perform cupping on seventeen or nineteen days. And twenty-one: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”"
"8255","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Omar bin Hafs bin Omar Al-Sadusi told us, Abd Al-Malik bin Abd Rabbuh Al-Ta’i told us, Abu Ali Othman bin Jafar, Muhammad bin Juhadah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar said to me: O Nafi’, I have become bleeding, so seek for me. Make him a cupper and make him a companion if you can, and do not make him an old man or a young boy, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Cupping on an empty stomach is better, and it contains blessings and healing. It increases the mind and increases the person’s memory, and cup yourselves with the blessing of God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection.” Thursday, and avoid Friday, Saturday, and Sunday, and cupping on Monday and Tuesday, for that is the day on which God has pardoned. Ayoub was afflicted with affliction, and neither leprosy nor leprosy appeared except on Wednesday and Wednesday night. Rather, Ayoub was afflicted on Wednesday.” The narrators of this hadith are all trustworthy, except for this Othman bin Jaafar, for I do not know him to be just or reliable.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8255 - He is weak"
"8256","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abu Muslim told us, Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Arqam, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever was cupped on the day On Wednesday and Saturday, he saw clarity, and he had no one to blame but himself.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8256 - Suleiman bin Arqam is abandoned"
"8257","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Dinar Al-Adl told us, Asad bin Khuzaymah told us, Ahmad bin Yunus told us, Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that Abu Hind, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gravely Of the pain he was suffering from, and he said: “If there is any good in what you treat with, then cupping.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it. \"\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8257 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"8258","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Yazid bin Zurayi told us. Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What an excellent medicine “Cupping makes the blood go away, clears the sight, and lightens the spine.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.\n[Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8258 - Incorrect"
"8259","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told me, and Muhammad bin Muhammad bin Raja Al-Isfaraini told us, they said: We told him: Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami, Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ Al-Thaqafi told us, my maternal uncle Al-Walid bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not force your patients to eat and drink, for God Almighty feeds them and gives them drink.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of transmission. Its narrators are all Madani, and they did not narrate it. We have in it the hadith of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, who was the only one to narrate it to Muhammad. Ibn Muhammad Ibn Al-Walid Al-Yashkuri on his authority \"\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8259 - True"
"8260","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the use of evil medicine.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not They take it out. The evil medicine is alcohol itself, without a doubt. “The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on the hadith of Al-Thawri and Shu’bah. On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, “God Almighty did not make your cure for what He has forbidden to you.” Muslim alone narrated a hadith Shu’bah, on the authority of Samak ibn Harb, on the authority of Alqamah ibn Wa’il, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that it is not a cure, but rather a disease.\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8260 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8261","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told me, Amr bin Hafs Al-Sadusi told us, Asim bin Ali told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Khalid, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Othman al-Taymi, who said: “A doctor mentioned medication with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He mentioned a frog used for medicine, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade killing it. This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Necessity led to the narration of the hadith of Al-Layth bin Abi Sulaym, may God have mercy on him, and he did not go on with what was mentioned above.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8261 - True"
"8262","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Yunus al-Qurashi told us, Bishr bin Hajar al-Sami told us, Fudayl bin Iyad told us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no one but And in his head there is a vein of leprosy oozing out, so if he is agitated, God will give him the cold, so do not treat him.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8262 - As if it were fabricated"
"8263","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari informed us about Marw, Abu Al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Abdul Hamid bin Saifi bin Abdullah bin Suhaib told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that Suhaib, may God be pleased with him, said: I came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, with dates and bread in his hands, so he said: “Come and eat.” So I took a bite of the dates, and he said: “Do you eat dates when you have ulcers?” So I said: O Messenger of God, I am chewing on the other side. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, smiled, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He brings him out.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8263 - True"
"8264","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Ammar bin Harun told us, Muhammad bin Ziyad al-Tahan told us, Maymoon bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Beware of sitting in the sun, for it It wears out the garment, makes the wind stink, and reveals the hidden disease.”\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8264 - This is from the position of the miller"
"8265","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shadhan al-Jawhari told us, Ubaid Allah bin Muhammad al-Qurashi told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Hammad bin Imran bin Musa bin Talha, Talha bin Yahya bin Talha told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Talha bin Ubaidullah, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he had a quince in his hand, and he threw it to me and said: “Shut it down, O Abu Muhammad, for it is too big.” \"heart\"\n[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8265 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
